  <data key="d17">StructuralState</data>
  <data key="d18">c-CoSe2/CoN heterointerface</data>
  <data key="d19">Heterointerface constructed by cubic-CoSe2 phase transition accompanied by in situ CoN formation.</data>
</node>
<node id="site_cose2_co">
  <data key="d17">ActiveSite</data>
  <data key="d18">Co site in c-CoSe2</data>
  <data key="d19">The cobalt site in cubic CoSe2 identified as the main active site for ORR/OER.</data>
</node>
<node id="factor_coordination_environment">
  <data key="d17">MechanisticFactor</data>
  <data key="d18">local coordination environment</data>
  <data key="d19">Local coordination environment modulated by heterostructure formation.</data>
</node>
<node id="factor_co_se_n_bond_lengths">
  <data key="d17">MechanisticFactor</data>
  <data key="d18">increased Co-Se/N bond lengths</data>
  <data key="d19">Increase in Co-Se/N bond lengths associated with heterostructure engineering.</data>
</node>
<node id="descriptor_co_d_orbital_structure">
  <data key="d17">Descriptor</data>
  <data key="d18">Co d-orbital electronic structure</data>
  <data key="d19">d-orbital electronic structure of Co in c-CoSe2, tailored by in situ CoN incorporation.</data>
</node>
<node id="descriptor_electronic_state_near_fermi">
  <data key="d17">Descriptor</data>
  <data key="d18">Co electronic state near the Fermi energy level</data>
  <data key="d19">Electronic state near the Fermi energy level associated with the main Co active site.</data>
</node>
<node id="calc_theoretical_orr_oer">
  <data key="d17">Calculation</data>
  <data key="d18">Theoretical ORR/OER calculations</data>
  <data key="d20">theoretical calculations</data>
  <data key="d21">[]</data>
  <data key="d22">The abstract states that theoretical calculations were used to examine the active site and thermodynamic barriers for ORR/OER.</data>
</node>
<node id="claim_cose2_co_active_site">
  <data key="d17">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d18">The Co site in c-CoSe2 is the main active site for ORR/OER.</data>
  <data key="d23">active-site assignment</data>
  <data key="d24">The Co site in c-CoSe2 is the main active site for ORR/OER.</data>
  <data key="d25">computational</data>
  <data key="d19">Theoretical calculations associate the main ORR/OER activity with a Co site in cubic CoSe2 having an electronic state near the Fermi energy level.</data>
</node>
<node id="claim_con_tailors_co_electronics">
  <data key="d17">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d18">In situ CoN incorporation energetically tailors the Co d-orbital electronic structure in the c-CoSe2/CoN heterostructure and lowers thermodynamic barriers for ORR/OER.</data>
  <data key="d23">electronic-structure mechanism</data>
  <data key="d24">In situ CoN incorporation energetically tailors the Co d-orbital electronic structure in the c-CoSe2/CoN heterostructure and lowers thermodynamic barriers for ORR/OER.</data>
  <data key="d25">computational</data>
  <data key="d19">This is the authors' theoretical interpretation of the effect of heterointerface engineering on bifunctional oxygen electrocatalysis.</data>
</node>
